Bit-fields in a class with base classes: the class must be padded (crash
otherwise); base padding components do not count as the derived class being
padded; padding names are made unique.
The expected sizes and offsets are those of the LP64 x86_64 data model
(`--64'); the test is not meaningful in a 32-bit configuration.
